  "id": "substitution",
  "term": "substitution",
  "definition": "In learning and perception research, substitution can mean using one kind of sensory input to stand in for information that is normally obtained in another way. In the packet’s example, vibration delivered to the fingers substitutes for direct distance information and can be learned well enough to support reaching and grasping, with practice transferring across device setups.",
